#
# The scores are a Stockfish 15 analysis of sixty seconds a position at
# multipv 10, which the source records line by line and is recorded here once.
#
# One position a line, as a four field fen followed by a bm operation holding
# the highest scoring move, or every one of them where several share the top
# score, an id operation naming the theme and the position within it, and a
# points operation holding every graded move with its score.
# The clocks are not part of it: every position is searched as if it had just
# arisen.
#
# A position is worth what the move the search settles on is worth, and
# nothing when that move is not one of the graded ones, so this suite says how
# good an answer was where the tactical one says whether it was the answer.
# Where several moves share the top score, bm names all of them, the way a
# tactical position with two ways to win does.
#
# Changing a line changes every total this suite has ever printed,
# so add to the end rather than edit.
